  "implementation": [
    "Authored source URIs and full owned UTF-16 frames remain raw until default, identity or Host policy is applied.",
    "Distinct frame-transform and logger continuations preserve buffering, reentry, rejection, pending roots and deprecation publication order.",
    "Diagnostic compression precedes transformation; each returned frame is checked before requesting the next callback.",
    "Callback-origin metadata distinguishes four actual failure phases without manufacturing Java exception classes.",
    "Foreign logger/transformer failures use the authored root declaration span while preserving real trace caller frames.",
    "Native, N-API and Wasm use the same engine and typed transport for arbitrary UTF-16 frames."
